From 463971752131058d551bf1d4c4d8b2acd13e7732 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude-edit@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 04:27:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(permissions): never truncate a request before deciding on
 it

authorize() cut each resource to 1,024 chars and the list to 16 before
classifying, fingerprinting and displaying it, while tools execute up to
8,000 chars / 32 files. Anything past the cut was never reviewed.

- reject over-limit requests (permission_resource_limit) instead of truncating
- fingerprint the whole request with SHA-256 over JSON
- agentPermissionResources() no longer pre-truncates provider requests
- the bash tool's length cap now uses the same constant as the permission layer
---
